.TH MV 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
mv \- move or rename files and directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mv
.RB [ \-fi ]
.I source ... destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mv
changes the name of a file.
If the new name is a directory, the file is moved to that directory
under its old name.
With several sources, the last operand must be a directory.
.PP
A move within one parent directory uses ProDOS RENAME.
Across directories or volumes, maux copies the data and then removes
the source. Directory trees are handled recursively; replacement of
a nonempty destination directory is refused.
.TP
.B \-f
Do not prompt before replacing an existing destination.
.TP
.B \-i
Prompt before replacement; only y or Y proceeds.
.PP
The last -i or -f wins. A declined move is not an error.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/MV  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cp(1), rm(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 for successful or declined moves, 1 for move failures, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
A cross-directory move is not atomic, even on one volume. A copy or source-removal failure can leave both source and destination; inspect both before retrying.
